/////////////////////////////////
// cp_trap_entry_spelp
//   With the landing pad enable of the mode set, trap from VS-mode and VU-mode into VS-mode (hedeleg[3] =
//   hedeleg[18] = 1) and into HS-mode (hedeleg = 0).  jalr through a non-link register to a non-LPAD
//   instruction traps with ELP = LP_EXPECTED, which the trap saves in vsstatus.SPELP or sstatus.SPELP.  The
//   handler's SRET restores it, so the next non-LPAD instruction traps again before the lpad.  An ebreak
//   that no indirect jump precedes traps with ELP = NO_LP_EXPECTED, so the instruction after it does not.
/////////////////////////////////
